IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `oas-core`
IMPORT `oas-core-measures`
IMPORT `oas-core-periods`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-eligibility`
IMPORT `oa2-part2-spouse`

-- Tests of oa2-part2-spouse: section 15. Every expected value is worked out by hand from the words of the section,
-- with the reasoning in the comment. The current payment period used throughout is July 1, 2022 to June 30, 2023.

`test current period` MEANS `s 10: the current payment period` (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1)
`test with` MEANS JUST `s 15: as though the person had a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`
`test without` MEANS JUST `s 15: as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner on the last day of the previous payment period`

§ `Section 15(1) and (1.1) -- what the applicant must state and tell`

#ASSERT `s 15(1): the person must state in the application whether the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner and, if so, who` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1): the person must state in the application whether the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner and, if so, who` FALSE
-- The window is the payment period and the month before it: June 1, 2022 to June 30, 2023.
#ASSERT `s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `test current period` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 6 1))
#ASSERT `s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `test current period` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 6 30))
#ASSERT `s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `test current period` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 6 30))
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `test current period` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 5 31))
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `test current period` (JUST (YearMonthDay 2023 7 1))
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1): the person has or had a spouse or common-law partner at a time in the window` `test current period` NOTHING
-- (1.1): waived under 11(4), no spouse before the last period with a supplement, a spouse now: all three.
#ASSERT `s 15(1.1): the person must notify the Minister without delay of the change` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1.1): the person must notify the Minister without delay of the change` FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1.1): the person must notify the Minister without delay of the change` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(1.1): the person must notify the Minister without delay of the change` TRUE TRUE FALSE

§ `Section 15(2) to (2.4) -- the spouse's statement`

-- Order of the inputs: has or had a spouse; (a) spouse filed a statement; (b) spouse's application received; (c) estimated
-- under 14(1.1); direction under (3); direction under (4.1); (4.2) applies.
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2): the application may be considered and dealt with` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(2.1): the Minister may waive the requirement to submit the information described in subsection 15(1)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.1): the Minister may waive the requirement to submit the information described in subsection 15(1)` FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2.2): the Minister may waive the requirement to file a statement under paragraph 15(2)(a)` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.2): the Minister may waive the requirement to file a statement under paragraph 15(2)(a)` FALSE
-- Filed, or waived (deemed filed): either; neither: not.
#ASSERT `s 15(2.2): the statement is filed or is deemed to have been filed` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(2.2): the statement is filed or is deemed to have been filed` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.2): the statement is filed or is deemed to have been filed` FALSE FALSE
-- (2.3): the Minister intends to waive under 11(3.1) AND the person has a spouse.
#ASSERT `s 15(2.3): the Minister must notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing and provide the information` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.3): the Minister must notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing and provide the information` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.3): the Minister must notify the spouse or common-law partner in writing and provide the information` FALSE TRUE
-- (2.4): the person born on May 12, 1957 attains 65 on May 12, 2022: the last day is May 11, 2022.
#ASSERT `s 15(2.4): the last day on which the spouse or common-law partner may file the statement correcting inaccuracies` (YearMonthDay 1957 5 12) EQUALS (YearMonthDay 2022 5 11)
#ASSERT `s 15(2.4): the spouse or common-law partner has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 5 11)) (YearMonthDay 1957 5 12)
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.4): the spouse or common-law partner has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 5 12)) (YearMonthDay 1957 5 12)
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(2.4): the spouse or common-law partner has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` TRUE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 1957 5 12)
-- Nothing inaccurate: nothing to correct.
#ASSERT `s 15(2.4): the spouse or common-law partner has complied with the duty to file a statement correcting inaccuracies` FALSE NOTHING (YearMonthDay 1957 5 12)

§ `Section 15(3) and (3.1) -- directions where there is no statement`

-- (3)(a): no statement or application filed by the spouse and no estimate: the Minister may. Either of them: not under (a).
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(a): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(3)(a): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(3)(a): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 15(3)(b): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(3)(b): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with as though the person did not have a spouse or common-law partner` FALSE
-- (3.1): the direction was made in the period of September 2021 (July 2021 to June 2022) and continues in every later
-- period unless cancelled.
#ASSERT `s 15(3.1): the treatment under a continuing direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(3.1): the treatment under a continuing direction` (YearMonthDay 2021 11 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(3.1): the treatment under a continuing direction` (YearMonthDay 2021 6 30) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(3.1): the treatment under a continuing direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 1) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(3.1): the treatment under a continuing direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2021 9 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15(3.2) to (4) -- the incarcerated spouse`

-- (3.2): satisfied; the month of release is December 2022: November may be directed; December may not.
#ASSERT `s 15(3.2): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with, for the month, as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 1) TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20))
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(3.2): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with, for the month, as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 1) TRUE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20))
#ASSERT `s 15(3.2): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with, for the month, as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 1) TRUE NOTHING
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(3.2): the Minister may direct that the application be dealt with, for the month, as though the applicant did not have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 1) FALSE NOTHING
-- (3.3): a direction first made for September 2022 continues until the month before the month of release (December).
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 8 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 9 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20)) EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20)) EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE FALSE (JUST (YearMonthDay 2022 12 20)) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Not released yet: it goes on. Cancelled: it does not. No direction: it does not.
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) TRUE TRUE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(3.3): the treatment under a continuing direction for an incarcerated person's spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 15) (YearMonthDay 2022 9 1) FALSE FALSE NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(4): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay of the release` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(4): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay of the release` FALSE

§ `Section 15(4.1) and (4.2) -- separation, and loss of a common-law partner`

-- (4.1): separated in January 2022; the three months after (February, March, April) make the third month April; the
-- person is treated as having ceased to have a spouse at the end of April, so May and later are calculated without.
#ASSERT `s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` (YearMonthDay 2022 5 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 1 15) EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` (YearMonthDay 2022 4 30) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 1 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` (YearMonthDay 2022 8 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 1 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A payment period that commences on or before June 30, 1999 is outside (4.1); one that commences on July 1, 1999 is in.
#ASSERT `s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` (YearMonthDay 2000 8 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 6 30) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(4.1): the treatment for a separated person` (YearMonthDay 2000 8 1) (YearMonthDay 1999 7 1) TRUE (YearMonthDay 2000 1 15) EQUALS `test without`
-- (4.2): the common-law partner is lost in October 2022 otherwise than by death; the third month following is January
-- 2023; February 2023 and later in the period are calculated without.
#ASSERT `s 15(4.2): the treatment after a common-law partner is lost otherwise than by death` (YearMonthDay 2023 2 1) `test current period` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) TRUE EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(4.2): the treatment after a common-law partner is lost otherwise than by death` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 31) `test current period` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(4.2): the treatment after a common-law partner is lost otherwise than by death` (YearMonthDay 2023 6 30) `test current period` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) TRUE EQUALS `test without`
-- A month after the period is not in "that payment period".
#ASSERT `s 15(4.2): the treatment after a common-law partner is lost otherwise than by death` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 1) `test current period` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(4.2): the treatment after a common-law partner is lost otherwise than by death` (YearMonthDay 2023 2 1) `test current period` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15(5) and (5.1) -- review of a direction`

-- (5): the period April 1, 1998 to June 30, 1999 ends before July 1, 1999. The review was made in September 1998 and the
-- direction specified that they were spouses: October 1998 is calculated with a spouse; September itself is not.
`test period 1998-99` MEANS `Calendar span` OF (YearMonthDay 1998 4 1), (YearMonthDay 1999 6 30)
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1998 10 1) `test period 1998-99` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) `test with` EQUALS `test with`
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1998 9 30) `test period 1998-99` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) `test with` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The direction may specify the other basis.
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1998 10 1) `test period 1998-99` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) `test without` EQUALS `test without`
-- A month after the period; a period that ends after June 30, 1999; no review; no basis specified: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1999 8 1) `test period 1998-99` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) `test with` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 2023 1 1) `test current period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 15) `test with` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1998 10 1) `test period 1998-99` FALSE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) `test with` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(5): the treatment under a reviewed direction for a payment period ending before July 1, 1999` (YearMonthDay 1998 10 1) `test period 1998-99` TRUE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING
-- (5.1): a (3)(a) direction was made, the spouse's statement was later filed, nothing else justifies the direction, the
-- review was completed in November 2022: December 2022 and later in the period are calculated with a spouse.
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 1) `test current period` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 20) EQUALS `test with`
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 30) `test current period` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 20) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 1) `test current period` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Some other reason for a direction under (3): the review does not reverse it.
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 1) `test current period` TRUE TRUE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 20) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 1) `test current period` FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 20) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 2022 12 1) `test current period` TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 11 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A period that commences on or before June 30, 1999 is (5)'s, not (5.1)'s.
#ASSERT `s 15(5.1): the treatment after the review of a direction` (YearMonthDay 1998 10 1) `test period 1998-99` TRUE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15(6.1) to (7.2) -- a spouse gained or lost during the period`

-- (6.1): a person who had no spouse before a month but has one at its end (paragraph (a)), began in September 2022:
-- October 2022 and later are calculated with a spouse; September is not.
#ASSERT `s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 20) EQUALS `test with`
#ASSERT `s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 9 30) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Paragraph (b) alone, and paragraph (c) alone, are enough; none of the three is not.
#ASSERT `s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) FALSE TRUE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 20) EQUALS `test with`
#ASSERT `s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) FALSE FALSE TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 20) EQUALS `test with`
#ASSERT `s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 1) (YearMonthDay 2022 7 1) FALSE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 9 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- A payment period that commences on or before June 30, 1999 is outside.
#ASSERT `s 15(6.1): the treatment after a person begins to have a spouse or common-law partner` (YearMonthDay 1998 10 1) (YearMonthDay 1998 4 1) TRUE FALSE FALSE (YearMonthDay 1998 9 20) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7.1): ceases to have a spouse in October 2022: November 2022 and later in the period are calculated without.
#ASSERT `s 15(7.1): the treatment after a person ceases to have a spouse` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 1) `test current period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(7.1): the treatment after a person ceases to have a spouse` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 31) `test current period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(7.1): the treatment after a person ceases to have a spouse` (YearMonthDay 2023 7 1) `test current period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(7.1): the treatment after a person ceases to have a spouse` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 1) `test current period` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (7.2): the common-law partner died in October 2022: the same.
#ASSERT `s 15(7.2): the treatment after a common-law partner dies` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 1) `test current period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15(7.2): the treatment after a common-law partner dies` (YearMonthDay 2022 10 31) `test current period` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15(7.2): the treatment after a common-law partner dies` (YearMonthDay 2022 11 1) `test current period` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2022 10 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Section 15(8) and (9) -- putting the treatments together, and the duty to inform`

-- None operates, or only one kind operates: that kind. Two kinds that disagree: NOTHING (fork F-15-1).
#ASSERT `s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` (LIST NOTHING, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` (LIST NOTHING, `test with`) EQUALS `test with`
#ASSERT `s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` (LIST `test without`, NOTHING, `test without`) EQUALS `test without`
#ASSERT `s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` (LIST `test with`, `test without`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 15: the treatment that the directions and deemings give for the month` (LIST `test without`, `test with`, NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
-- (9): any one of separating, ceasing to have a spouse, or having one at the start of this month but not the last.
#ASSERT `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 15(9): the applicant must inform the Minister without delay` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE
